{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations","id":1066765,"title":"Dragon-Blooded families, lifespans and generations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-23T03:53:13-07:00","id":1066765,"title":"Dragon-Blooded families, lifespans and generations","content":"So, sometimes I think about the the idea of &quot;generations&quot; of Dragon-Blooded, and it seems really weird. The social expectation (in the Realm, at least) is that they have a child every 5 years or so, right? Let's say 1 in 5 exalts, and ignore the other 4 because they're not relevant to this. Then the children have kids, and so on, and so on. The original couple is 200 years old, they have 8 generations of children. The 7th generation are adults. You could be the youngest adult generation, and go attend your great-great-great-great-great-aunt's birth.<br /> <br /> Do you give much thought to the kind of familial relationships that yields? Is the concept of a &quot;generation&quot; in any way meaningful at this point? How do you refer to your relatives? Do you call a nephew &quot;uncle&quot; because he's 100 years older than you and it's weird?<br /> <br /> I try to imagine this in detail sometimes, but to be honest it kind of does my head in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5716-thousand_comforts_base","name":"Thousand_Comforts_Base","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T04:43:54-07:00","id":1066773,"title":"","content":"The Dynasty is aristocracy writ large, sprawling cats-cradle family trees are the norm. The good news is that if someone isn't a direct-line relative they are usually some kind of cousin, so that's a fairly reliable way to refer to extended relatives. <br /> <br /> As an aside, I think it would be an excellent idea to ignore the prior social guidelines on having of children every five years or whatever it is. Dynasts have a social expectation to have heirs, the same as any aristocracy, but the social pressure to just <i>have more children</i> creates the mistaken impression that numbers are the primary goal. I have seen people unironically refer to female Dragon-Bloods as &quot;baby factories&quot; and I never want to see it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T04:50:20-07:00","id":1066776,"title":"","content":"5 years isn't the recommended frequency anyway. It's the <i>fastest</i> they can manage without causing health problems. The average is said to be about 8 per century, or one every <i>twelve</i> years on the next line. Which is possibly still a bit high.<br /> <br /> Oh, also they're not expected to actually marry and start having kids until they're, like, 50 or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-23-2017, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:04:28-07:00","id":1066779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1066773#post1066773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have seen people unironically refer to female Dragon-Bloods as &quot;baby factories&quot; and I never want to see it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, look, that is pretty gross, I think we're on the same page there. I tend to picture the superhuman capacity of the Dragon-Blooded quashing that view of them, but I admit that's part of a deliberate attempt on my part to interpret Creation as less sexist than the real world.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm mainly wondering if people see opportunities for bizarre kinds of intrigue that become possible when people are able to produce children for 250 years straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5716-thousand_comforts_base","name":"Thousand_Comforts_Base","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:07:19-07:00","id":1066781,"title":"","content":"There's also the point about how bringing up children in the Scarlet Dynasty, even before certainty that they're going to be Exalted, is something that is a significant expense by design, a matter that will both limit how many children any given couple has and how long they need to wait before starting. I assume that it tends to average out to something like most Dynasts only having children at all between the ages of 100 and 200.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere are certainly going to be occasions where generations overlap, but probably not something as extreme as the distant ancestor of a Dynast still having children by the time that Dynast becomes an adult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dynasts have a social expectation to have heirs, the same as any aristocracy</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd note that the dynamic there is something like a cross between aristocratic conventions and 1930s fascist ideas about children as the next generation of soldiers for the fatherland. Probably helped by the apparent fact that the Scarlet Dynasty is an aristocracy distinctly not really made wealthy by straightforward income from land ownership, as well as the fact that their Great House structure is a lot more expansive and communal than a lot of real-world aristocracies have been; a child of a Great House is not exactly in line to anything specifically descending from their own parents, even if those are the people with primary responsibility for making sure that you're properly educated and arrange your starting political contacts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:36:56-07:00","id":1066818,"title":"","content":"I feel like I've read from someone official that the number of children a Dynast has is going to be fewer than was implied in 2e, not least because of how incredibly <i>expensive</i> the education of a Dynastic heir is. Like, on one hand, yes, having more children (especially those who become Exalted) is a prestigious thing, to have more than a handful of children will bankrupt your average Dynast. I would imagine there are some exceptions - Mnemon herself, for instance, strikes me as the sort of woman who would be able to have more than the three to five children I typically envision Dynasts having. On the other hand, she's also the sort of woman who would only have children (at this point in her life) if, for some reason, she felt as though she needed a direct child, rather than using one of her doubtless numerous descendants.<br /> <br /> I believe this expenditure would also mean that the non-Exalted Dynasts are going to be seen as more prominent in 3e - that is, even apart from the fact that the Immaculate Order would recognize them as almost as spiritually perfect as Dragon-Blooded, they are <i>still</i> amongst the best educated, trained, and nourished mortals in Creation. This is not to say they're not going to be looked down on by their families - especially if such expenditure is indeed the case. &quot;Do you <i>know</i> how much we spent on you, and you didn't even become Chosen?&quot; But still, I would imagine that they're not ignored the way they were in 2e.<br /> <br /> I would also imagine that not every child of a given pairing (even if the pairing is of two Dragon-Blooded) is Chosen - which would mean that they'd die within a century of being born. I would say that that lifetime would be time for the parents to recoup the financial losses of educating said mortal, but then you also should factor in that the mortal would probably have children of his or her own, which would also need the exorbitant amounts of money involved, so perhaps not. In any case, I'm imagining that most couples probably only deliberately have a handful of children at any one time - though there will be exceptions for exceptionally wealthy individuals and possibly even Houses. Like, I imagine that Ragara and Cynis both tend towards having more children than, say, Cathak or Tepet (back when Tepet wasn't on the decline), because they're both known for being wealthy even amongst the Dynasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:55:03-07:00","id":1066830,"title":"","content":"I went with the notion it wasn't a good thing to have too many extra Dragonblooded hanging around. There is only so many heirloom artifacts and titles to go around. If you are the youngest Dragonblooded in your family and your older brother and sister got all the good stuff, what's an entitled Dynast going to do? Cause problems and maybe throw in with that Anathema dude who is threatening to bring the system down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:15:13-07:00","id":1066930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1066830#post1066830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went with the notion it wasn't a good thing to have too many extra Dragonblooded hanging around. There is only so many heirloom artifacts and titles to go around. If you are the youngest Dragonblooded in your family and your older brother and sister got all the good stuff, what's an entitled Dynast going to do? Cause problems and maybe throw in with that Anathema dude who is threatening to bring the system down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am personally fond of the &quot;heir and spare&quot; idea, a Dynast couple does not really have to worry about loosing children to miscarriage or disease like actual nobles would have so they would have little need to <i>constantly </i>give birth. It would make more sense if they strive to keep at least one heir and an extra in case the first one is dumb enough to get themselves killed. Also it makes them not too essential if they start getting ideas about getting their inheritance early. Whats interesting is that if males and females inherit on equal basis it becomes exponentially easier to keep a stable succession.<br /> <br /> Btw vast age differences were not exactly rare in most historical aristocracies so it was not altogether that strange to attend to the birth of sibling that would be younger than your own child. The closeness in families also varied quite a bit so I would really like to see a more pronounced difference in this attitude amongst the houses (if I recall correctly 2ed only had differing tiers of neglect supplemented by an army of tutors).<br /> <br /> On that note have we ever seen an inheritance scheme for Dynasts? For titles and land (since the way evocations work makes keeping all the artifacts together more than a little useless given how much effort it takes to master even one) since Partible Inheritance would subdivide the realm into oblivion within a few centuries I imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 03-23-2017, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:17:50-07:00","id":1066933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thousand_Comforts_Base</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1066779#post1066779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm mainly wondering if people see opportunities for bizarre kinds of intrigue that become possible when people are able to produce children for 250 years straight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, especially with inheritances.<br /> <br /> It's just another garnish on the intrigue from cadet branches of the family, main-line vs. off-line, adopted vs. trueborn, married-in fathers from the currently hated house vs. fathers from the currently allied house promoting their kids over others, and any other kind of label dissonance that is so important in the lives of aristocrats. And that's just the blood-related intrigue. We haven't even gotten to money or land or politics. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:21:49-07:00","id":1066937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1066930#post1066930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note have we ever seen an inheritance scheme for Dynasts? For titles and land...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I really want one. I've leaned on the European norms I know best (gender-flipped, of course, just like matriarchal marriage is the norm I expect the same in inheritance). <br /> <br /> But I'd be interested in some Eastern variations being thrown in given Exalted's influences. I just don't know them well enough to make them up myself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:22:13-07:00","id":1066982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1066818#post1066818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">to have more than a handful of children will bankrupt your average Dynast.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHeh, I imagine that it's actually fairly difficult to actually bankrupt a Dynast, if one considers the technical definition of bankruptcy as being fundamentally incapable of paying off your debts, rather than the colloquial use of having no money.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich informs the matter of how I would say that it's likely that the majority of Dynasts who wouldn't need to go into debt to be able to afford the added expenses of tutors and school dues are the ones who are already past the point in their lives when they have children. Which is to say, if you're rich enough to be able to pay for the schooling of Dynast children, you're probably in a venerable position in which you pay for the schooling of <i>other people's</i> children.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen one might consider the range of ways in which Dynasts could pay off a debt in a non-monetary fashion, to older Dynasts who can probably absorb monetary losses without much trouble but see a lot to want out of having somebody who can be sent to murder an enemy, go off on an adventure to reclaim your fallen Brother's daiklave, or give you very high consideration for the child benefiting from that loan being married to one of your granddaughters.<br /> <br /> \u200bI imagine that for a Dynast to actually go bankrupt, you either have to be monumentally bad with your money, or have incurred a lot of bad blood from your peers, while also being the kind of person whose principles won't let you accept bailouts from the Guild or opportunistic spirits and Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note have we ever seen an inheritance scheme for Dynasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Exalted: the Dragon Blooded, page 107:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dragon-Blooded do not count on inheritances. Their parents tend to live so long and beget so many offspring that inheritances are rare and generally insignificant. When there is an inheritance, half of it goes to the spouse or eldest Dragon-Blooded child. Another 40 percent is divided between all remaining Dragon- Blooded children. The final 10 percent is divided up between all mortal children.<br /> ~~<br /> In theory, a Dragon-Blooded may leave behind a will that overrides the official inheritance percentages. In practice, most wills are conveniently lost or damaged, while others are blatantly ignored. If the will slights a Dragon-Blooded in favour of a patrician, most imperial judges will take any half-formed excuse to rule it invalid. </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that was repeated verbatim somewhere in Second Edition, but don't care to look for it.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For titles and land</div> </div> </div> </div>It appears to me that members of the Scarlet Dynasty don't actually have titles, and that what lends they had under the Empress were more like something that they held in trust from a nationalised scheme, rather than being individual possessions.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">since the way evocations work makes keeping all the artifacts together more than a little useless given how much effort it takes to master even one</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, you're kind of begging the question there of why somebody even has multiple Artifacts to distribute among children in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bI imagine that the hereditary Artifacts are often something that are passed on while a venerable and retired Dynast is still alive, and are based more on personal judgements and relationships, rather than legal constrictions.<br /> <br /> \u200bReally, when you're liable to have a number of children of superhuman prowess at the same time, the idea of giving arbitrary special treatment to the one who happens to have been born first for anything of significance (rather than what is left in your bank account after your debts are paid off following your death) seems a bit odd.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn any case, the overall attitude of the Scarlet Dynasty seems to be that you have to go out and actually make something of yourself, earning your own way up, rather than waiting more than a hundred years for your parents to die.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:31:35-07:00","id":1066999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1066830#post1066830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are the youngest Dragonblooded in your family and your older brother and sister got all the good stuff, what's an entitled Dynast going to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Be Cathak Cainan?<br /> <br /> \u200bI admit, that's a bit facetious; Cainan has three Exalted younger siblings, in addition to the three older ones<br /> <br /> \u200bThe point is, exactly what did these older siblings do that you didn't that let them get all of the good stuff?<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, whom did they get it from?<br /> <br /> \u200bThese people do have jobs, don't they?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:34:49-07:00","id":1067040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1066999#post1066999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThese people do have jobs, don't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading has been that the House or branch of the House does a lot of supporting for a Dynast. The non-exalted Dynasts will use their training to enter the Thousand Scales or Immaculate Order (or serve the house directly as functionaries, bureaucrats, or low level officers), helping to support their House's economic/political/military machine. This lets the Dragonblooded focus on honing particular skills to super-human levels with a stipend from the House, and the understanding that they owe the House service and loyalty. Those who don't want that level of obligation or don't feel like their house is offering the proper level of support (or are instructed to do so by the house) join one of the Realm's many institutions to work their way up. And if they really want to shrug all that off, well, they can party in the Threshold for a couple of years. <br /> <br /> That's the sort of level where most Dragonblooded will be trying to make their fortunes and names, not waiting for inheritances. They gain institutional wealth and power by serving their house and rising up through its ranks. If an elder Dynast is retiring from the Legions and none of his direct descendants are Chosen or lack martial inclinations, he can send his hereditary daiklave to one of his sister's grandkids. A DB who focuses on perfecting art can live a comfortable life on the House's dime, while a Dynast who learns to craft artifacts can generate enormous wealth and prosperity for his House and rise through the ranks on their own merits. Parents will try and promote their own children--it's only natural, after all--and intrigue will arise out of that, but I view the wealth of Dynasts as institutions rather than inheritances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:13:01-07:00","id":1067078,"title":"","content":"The Realm can always use as many dragonblooded as it can get, but it needs well-cultivated dynasts even more than it needs raw numbers. A proper dynast is defined by more than just their exaltation; they've been raised all their life to support and perpetuate their society. Ideal dynasts have to possess a broad general education, specialized training in a career useful to the Empire, and at least a basic level of skill in the matters of governance and administration that come with a noble's rank. They need to be steeped in Realm culture, indoctrinated with its values, and bound to the Empire by ties of loyalty and ambition. Beyond all this, they must be instilled with the desire to start a family of their own and repeat the process with their own children. <br /> <br /> Dynasts, like knights, samurai, and other versions of the warrior-noble archetype, represent a massive investment of resources by their society. Having more fledgeling terrestrials than you have the resources to properly raise doesn't do you many favors as a family or as a great house. Compare the way Lost Eggs are treated in the Scarlet Empire; their assimilation into society is a trial by fire that's designed to make them immediately useful with a minimum of cost and effort. If all the Realm needed was raw numbers of exalts, they could train a much larger number of them by using similar methods. Instead, terrestrial households invest a great deal in a smaller number of children, because one well-trained dynast is worth more to them (and to the Realm) than two or three dragonblooded who are merely soldiers. <br /> <br /> As I've run the Realm in my own games, the greatly extended timeline of a dynast's life changes how they might view family. If you're a young scion of a dynastic family, your closest sibling in age might well be more than a decade older than you, and already beginning their career by the time you're in school. You'd probably end up bonding more with the other dynastic children closer to your age, regardless of whether they're technically your cousin, your nephew, or your great uncle. I imagine that actual terms of relation used would have more to do with relative age than with generation. Parent/grandparent/greatgrandparent would still work fine, though household heads and others with a sufficiently large pool of descendents would probably be referred to more by a name or absolute title. The equivalent term to Uncle, Aunt, etc would mean &quot;Relative who is older than me and who I am not descended from.&quot; Cousin makes a good term for a relative of similar age to you. Niece/Nephew is what you call anyone who'd call you Aunt/Uncle. Memorizing your exact relation to dozens or hundreds of different relatives is probably part of the tedious homework that every dynastic child goes through, because specific bloodlines are Important even if they're also massively inconvenient to day to day life. <br /> <br /> Overall, though, I don't imagine most of these terms to be quite as important to a dynast's day-to-day life as they are to us. The answer to &quot;What do you call your great grandfather's second son who is the same age as your dad and thus 60 years older than you&quot; is probably &quot;My Lord.&quot; Same goes for your sister's son who is nonetheless 80 years older than you. Most people who aren't your direct ancestors or descendants are probably just other members of the same great house from your perspective, and above or below you in the house hierarchy based on relative age and prestige. I can see complications arising from issues like whether a 40 year-old child of the household head ranks above a 100 year old child of a distant branch family, but overall the Realm's extended family ties, while highly important to society, don't seem to carry a lot of actual intimacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12562-winterwombat","name":"WinterWombat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:06:21-07:00","id":1067197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1066773#post1066773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, I think it would be an excellent idea to ignore the prior social guidelines on having of children every five years or whatever it is. Dynasts have a social expectation to have heirs, the same as any aristocracy, but the social pressure to just <i>have more children</i> creates the mistaken impression that numbers are the primary goal. I have seen people unironically refer to female Dragon-Bloods as &quot;baby factories&quot; and I never want to see it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, where did you get all of that from? According to both First and Second Edition (MoEP: Dragon Blooded pages 21-22), in the Realm Dragon Blood couples are expected to have at least 1 child every 50 years. Once the couple has had two children, the &quot;procreative&quot; requirement on their marriage is considered done, and they don't have to have any more children. So yeah, 2 kids in 100 years.<br /> <br /> It seems like you're complaining about something that was never in the gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:42:25-07:00","id":1067213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067197#post1067197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems like you're complaining about something that was never in the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIn fairness, details of the Realm's Exalted society were very elaborate even before the way some of them were mixed around between Editions; I think it's very easy to get them mixed up.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading has been that the House or branch of the House does a lot of supporting for a Dynast. The non-exalted Dynasts will use their training to enter the Thousand Scales or Immaculate Order (or serve the house directly as functionaries, bureaucrats, or low level officers), helping to support their House's economic/political/military machine. This lets the Dragonblooded focus on honing particular skills to super-human levels with a stipend from the House, and the understanding that they owe the House service and loyalty. Those who don't want that level of obligation or don't feel like their house is offering the proper level of support (or are instructed to do so by the house) join one of the Realm's many institutions to work their way up. And if they really want to shrug all that off, well, they can party in the Threshold for a couple of years.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bTo be sure, Exalted: the Dragon Blooded described the Dynasty in terms of about half of them having jobs in various institutions such as the military, the government, a family business or a prestigious craft, and the other half as being people like artists, explorers, adventurers and socialites, who I also presume live largely off of their portion of the family stipend in combination with some degree of patronage and debt or (in the case of the adventurers) being out in the world and acquiring wealth through things like rewards, raids and gambling.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm just making the point about how hardly anybody is just sitting on a rent-generating estate.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, even if they were, a lot of that still answers the question of what the youngest one does in the event of not getting an inheritance; go out into the world and be Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat goes with how my own reading of how the practice of newly graduated Exalted boarding with a relative outside of their parent's home will basically act as the older, more established one's agent, and how these younger people are probably generally going to be the model that people actually play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:53:27-07:00","id":1067220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067213#post1067213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIn fairness, details of the Realm's Exalted society were very elaborate even before the way some of them were mixed around between Editions; I think it's very easy to get them mixed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this was just the case of the the echo-chamber, where one guys mistakenly says something wrong, and then lots of other people take that as fact and run with it. So you have some guy saying the books present Dragon Blooded women as broodmares because for whatever reason he thinks that's what the books said. Then you have lots of other people who don't bother looking in the books themselves and just take that guy's statement as fact. Then someone repeats it later, others think it's true and then people get mad at the books and demand the books get changed, when in fact that was never in the books to begin with.<br /> <br /> There were issues with Dragon Blooded and the Realm, but the idea that a couple is expected to have at least two children, one every half-century, never really struck me as overly problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T16:24:46-07:00","id":1067230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067220#post1067220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There were issues with Dragon Blooded and the Realm, but the idea that a couple is expected to have at least two children, one every half-century</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell... that is the bare minimum, which alone is reason enough to assume that many will have expectations a fair bit above it, before one gets to details such as having so few children being liable to hurt one financially.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlus there's the context in which those particular details are presented, where the focus is less on &quot;this is the minimum that you have to fulfil&quot; and more on &quot;these are the conditions under which your marriage will be automatically or voluntarily dissolved by the state&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T16:32:10-07:00","id":1067233,"title":"","content":"I mean, I imagine that the House as an institution owns all the family's assets, and the leader(s) (the Tepet council, Mnemon herself, Cathak Cainan) decide who is responsible for administering what. Forming a separate household probably yields a measure of autonomy. I took the talk of stipends being used to discourage unwanted behaviour (like marrying mortals) to imply that &quot;The House's money&quot; is distributed the same way as assets &amp; responsibility, no doubt with a fair bit of favouritism involved.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that a Dragon-Blood is an asset worth considerable expense, and even the poorer Great Houses can afford it. I'd expect that if a dynasty reached the point where they felt they had so many Dragon-Blooded children that there were no viable endeavours they could worthily occupy them with (which seems unlikely), it would've been within the Empress' interests to give that house some new source of revenue that would require a lot of work. That way she can ensure the continued steady growth of the Dragon-Blooded host. Unless she wanted to deliberately constrain that house's power, of course. Since her disappearance, the threat of civil war might make some more conservative, wanting to keep funds for legions, or quite the opposite, if they think there's time for a child to be Exalted and educated before open war breaks out. Or if they anticipate that the war will drag on.<br /> <br /> The existence of evocations does seem to undermine the idea that the Great Houses have an arsenal of artifact weapons &amp; armour that they move around as needs/whims dictate. I'd be surprised if that remains in 3e.<br /> <br /> AnubisXy - I can't find the bit where I read that &quot;5 year&quot; guideline. I'd concede that maybe I was in error, but Elfive's response sounds like they read the exact same thing that I did. Maybe they can point to it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5716-thousand_comforts_base","name":"Thousand_Comforts_Base","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:18:23-07:00","id":1067249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067230#post1067230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWell... that is the bare minimum, which alone is reason enough to assume that many will have expectations a fair bit above it, before one gets to details such as having so few children being liable to hurt one financially.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlus there's the context in which those particular details are presented, where the focus is less on &quot;this is the minimum that you have to fulfil&quot; and more on &quot;these are the conditions under which your marriage will be automatically or voluntarily dissolved by the state&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of reasons, both positive and negative, that would encourage families to have children. The minimum is 2 children over the course of 100 years is a far cry from the Realm treating Dragon Blooded women like &quot;baby factories.&quot; The most typical number of children that families choose to have is around one child every 25-30 years, so on average anywhere from 4-8 children over the course of the 200 years, though of course if a family wants less they will have less, and families who want more will have somewhat more.<br /> <br /> And really, even the &quot;typical&quot; number of children (two every 50 years) seems perfectly reasonable. Having two children over the course of 50 years is fairly normal in many real-life cultures. Regardless, any Dragon Blooded woman who <i>is</i> treated like a baby factory is very much an exception rather than a general representative of the Realm.<br /> <br /> To Thousand Comforts - I have no clue where the &quot;every five years&quot; comes from. I've never seen anything about that in the game line before. The closest I can think of is the &quot;Too Many Children&quot; sidebar in 1st edition Dragon Blooded, about a woman, Tepet Lesarl who managed to have one child every two years for 20 years straight (so 10 children). She ended up dying just after her 100th birthday. It's a cautionary tale and was included in part to explain why the Realm specifically <i>does not</i> pursue a policy of demanding that couples pump out as many babies as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:34:43-07:00","id":1067257,"title":"","content":"Ok, I think that must be where I got it - I remembered it as her keeping up 1 child every 2 years for the whole century, and that being why they didn't expect more than 1 every 5 years, but I don't have a copy of 1e Dragon-Blooded handy to verify it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5716-thousand_comforts_base","name":"Thousand_Comforts_Base","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T00:54:26-07:00","id":1067439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067197#post1067197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, where did you get all of that from? According to both First and Second Edition (MoEP: Dragon Blooded pages 21-22), in the Realm Dragon Blood couples are expected to have at least 1 child every 50 years. Once the couple has had two children, the &quot;procreative&quot; requirement on their marriage is considered done, and they don't have to have any more children. So yeah, 2 kids in 100 years.<br /> <br /> It seems like you're complaining about something that was never in the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was responding to what OP said, I was assuming I had missed something from 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T01:01:26-07:00","id":1067440,"title":"","content":"Ok, even if my numbers are definitively proven to be baseless, (which may happen, if so my bad,) it'd still be cool to hear people's ideas about intrigue in families where you can be 100 years older than your aunts &amp; uncles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5716-thousand_comforts_base","name":"Thousand_Comforts_Base","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T01:25:38-07:00","id":1067448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067197#post1067197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, where did you get all of that from? According to both First and Second Edition (MoEP: Dragon Blooded pages 21-22), in the Realm Dragon Blood couples are expected to have at least 1 child every 50 years. Once the couple has had two children, the &quot;procreative&quot; requirement on their marriage is considered done, and they don't have to have any more children. So yeah, 2 kids in 100 years.<br /> <br /> It seems like you're complaining about something that was never in the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the same source, but a different section. The Realm's familial obligation is two children within 50 years of marriage and no more than fifty years between children thereafter, or the marriage is dissolved. Later the book discusses the biology.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manual of Exalted Power: The Dragon Blooded, page 22</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among the Terrestrial Exalted, producing children is almost compulsory. The more children a couple produces, the more chance there is that one of the offspring will grow up to be another member of the Dragon-Blooded Host. Some Terrestrial women are known to take particular delight in producing child after child, although physicians have learned that Dragon-Blooded women need <i>at least five years between children.</i> Otherwise, it starts to age them unnaturally quickly. <i>The average number of births is eight per century</i>, or about one every 12 years. A Dragon-Blooded <i>pregnancy lasts a full 15-month year</i>. Given the sturdiness of Terrestrial physiology, a pregnancy only begins to show after five months, and an expectant mother may remain as active as normal for the first 12 months of pregnancy, with no significant danger to herself or the unborn child.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a social minimum rate of one child every fifty years, a biological maximum rate of one every five years, and averaging out to one every twelve years. Per couple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 03-24-2017, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T01:45:32-07:00","id":1067455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thousand_Comforts_Base</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1066779#post1066779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, look, that is pretty gross, I think we're on the same page there. I tend to picture the superhuman capacity of the Dragon-Blooded quashing that view of them, but I admit that's part of a deliberate attempt on my part to interpret Creation as less sexist than the real world.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm mainly wondering if people see opportunities for bizarre kinds of intrigue that become possible when people are able to produce children for 250 years straight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am currently enjoying playing a young Prince of the Earth Aisa competing with her grandmother Mnemon over great-grandmother's inheritance (the throne). Aisa's mother, in a shocking betrayal, sold Aisa's secrets to <i>her </i>mother rather than side with her daughter. Aisa also loves to refer to V'Neef as 'aunt', even though 'great aunt' is more correct. Reminding people of her bloodline is a statement, sometimes subtle and sometimes blunt, that even though she's young it's best not to underestimate her.<br /> <br /> Playing up the family angle in the conflict is all sorts of fun (and gets me an extra die in most social situations due to the Family background). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T02:36:26-07:00","id":1067465,"title":"","content":"I borrowed a 1e Dragon-Blooded book &amp; found the relevant section, I was misremembering this bit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted: the Dragon-Blooded</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...The average across the Realm is eight per century - about one every 12 years.<br /> <br /> Couples particularly eager to take advantage of the monetary and political gains to be had through children might have them as often as every five years...</div> </div> </div> </div>So anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067455#post1067455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am currently enjoying playing a young Prince of the Earth Aisa competing with her grandmother Mnemon over great-grandmother's inheritance (the throne). Aisa's mother, in a shocking betrayal, sold Aisa's secrets to <i>her </i>mother rather than side with her daughter. Aisa also loves to refer to V'Neef as 'aunt', even though 'great aunt' is more correct. Reminding people of her bloodline is a statement, sometimes subtle and sometimes blunt, that even though she's young it's best not to underestimate her.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite a pedigree! Your mum sounds like a jerk though. Maybe you should &quot;provide a concrete advantage against your (grand)mother&quot; like that Prefect at the start of Chapter 6 in the Compass of Celestial Directions: The Blessed Isle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5716-thousand_comforts_base","name":"Thousand_Comforts_Base","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T03:22:41-07:00","id":1067471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067249#post1067249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The minimum is 2 children over the course of 100 years is a far cry from the Realm treating Dragon Blooded women like &quot;baby factories.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, I of all people am the one advocating for the position of Terrestrial Exalted women as baby factories. Come on!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And really, even the &quot;typical&quot; number of children (two every 50 years) seems perfectly reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I am going to say it directly; neither of the Editions portrayed this as typical; they portrayed it as averaging out to one every twelve years, which is still nicely short of some rather repellent arguments. However many every fifty years is the minimum obligation to not have one's marriage dissolved, and something that is highly consistent with the culture of the Scarlet Dynasty as written treating as a subject of derision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Manual of Exalted Power: The Dragon Blooded</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, it has been a while since I read that one, I wonder if-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Terrestrial women are known to take particular delight in producing child after child </div> </div> </div>\u200bGrrrrraaaAAAARRGGHHH-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dragon-Blooded women need <i>at least five years between children.</i> Otherwise, it starts to age them unnaturally quickly </div> </div> </div>\u200bstupid stupid <i>stupid</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:39:45-07:00","id":1067678,"title":"","content":"By the way, the bit I was referring to in my post was indeed the section form MOEP: DB that Greyman quoted.<br /> <br /> I choose to assume the sprog-happy terrestrial women mentioned are minmaxing for Dynasty charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:04:07-07:00","id":1067695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thousand_Comforts_Base</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067440#post1067440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it'd still be cool to hear people's ideas about intrigue in families where you can be 100 years older than your aunts &amp; uncles.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm worried that saying so might come across as being a bit anti-fun, but I honestly feel as though in a system such as this, much younger people who are technically siblings of your parents are going to be treated in essentially the same way as cousins. I don't think any Dynast ten-year olds are going to invoke any cutesy authority over technically being your uncle or anything. I feel as though in a case such as this, their technical relationship to you matters less than where they fall in the conventional age ranges of Dynastic life; still expected to be disciplined in their schooling up until the point where they become fresh up and comers who are ready to serve as agents for established Dynasts.<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, even if the Dynasty operated on a system of familiar agnatic primogeniture, a much younger aunt or uncle still falls lower on the line of succession than you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:10:29-07:00","id":1067898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067471#post1067471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GrrrrraaaAAAARRGGHHH-<br /> <br /> stupid stupid <i>stupid</i></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Meh.</i> It is just saying &quot;Even if some ladies like being mothers, they are <i>not </i>baby-factories.&quot; They reason given is not the greatest, but not terra-bad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:29:41-07:00","id":1067906,"title":"","content":"The reason I hate the line about some Exalted being super enthusiastic about carrying children is that certain individuals have used it as the basis for noxious positions concerning how the Dragon Blooded wouldn't [I]really/I] have personal objections to somebody trying to regiment them into programs intended to create more Exalted en masse.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe reason that I dislike the line about how having children too often drains the life out of you is because it artlessly conflates two separate details from the First Edition book (the idea that it takes twice as long for them to recover from pregnancies as mortals, and an anecdote about a specific individual who was able to have children frequently and died early <i>because she had implicitly used sorcery to make herself age more quickly</i>), which I disdainfully associate with really weird arguments about how Authochthon clearly doesn't understand how biological reproduction works or has some deep thematic dissonance with it that is also the reason why the only way for Alchemicals to reproduce is via Voidtech and {gnashing teeth}.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T22:04:40-07:00","id":1067920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067898#post1067898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Meh.</i> It is just saying &quot;Even if some ladies like being mothers, they are <i>not </i>baby-factories.&quot; They reason given is not the greatest, but not terra-bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it comes across somewhat different. It sounds more like &quot;exalted mothers are baby factories, and this is their maximum output rate&quot;, and I absolutely see why that doesn't sit right with many people.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T23:35:39-07:00","id":1067934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067898#post1067898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Meh.</i> <br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> They reason given is not the greatest, but not terra-bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>This post about how insulting something is to women, brought to you by a [grey] man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-25-2017, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T04:04:32-07:00","id":1067955,"title":"","content":"I mean, the five year thing sounds like an <i>attempt</i> to dissuade from the whole &quot;baby factory&quot; thing to me, but not a particularly good one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T06:00:55-07:00","id":1067983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067906#post1067906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> which I disdainfully associate with really weird arguments about how Authochthon clearly doesn't understand how biological reproduction works or has some deep thematic dissonance with it that is also the reason why the only way for Alchemicals to reproduce is via Voidtech and {gnashing teeth}.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good.<br /> The point of that absurd argument was to highlight problems in MoEP: Dragon-Blooded which nobody seemed to give a shit about by footing the blame to Autochthon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T06:48:53-07:00","id":1067994,"title":"","content":"I mean, there has to be <i>some</i> differences between how dragonblooded reproduction works and how it works in real like because IRL finite eggs are a thing, so the only way to avoid them going through the menopause at what is for them a really young age is either to say that they get infinitely renewing eggs or drastically reduce the frequency of periods, which would mean the window for conception would be so difficult to hit randomly that they'd probably have to go into heat or something, which is just opening an entirely <i>new</i> can of worms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T07:17:30-07:00","id":1067999,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there's some sufficiently simple way to handwave the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T07:30:06-07:00","id":1068004,"title":"","content":"I don't give it a lot of thought, but my guess would be that their ovaries produce new eggs; a more gender-neutral (and to me, more interesting) biological factor to question with regard to Exalts is <i>teeth</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bHow long does a given tooth last in an Exalt's head? Once it's gone, is it gone forever, or will a new one grow given time? If it's the former, it'd either have to be absurdly durable, or elder Exalts<i> will</i> need some dentures; if it's the latter, how long does it take?<br /> <br /> \u200b(Though if you're not worried about teeth, you probably shouldn't be worried about eggs. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"159\" data-vbnamecard=\"159\">Leetsepeak</a> said, handwaving is pretty simple.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-25-2017, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T07:41:49-07:00","id":1068007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1068004#post1068004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does a given tooth last in an Exalt's head? Once it's gone, is it gone forever, or will a new one grow given time? If it's the former, it'd either have to be absurdly durable, or elder Exalts<i> will</i> need some dentures; if it's the latter, how long does it take?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think thats is almost always covered by their healing factor. If a tooth gets knocked out, then they are simply healed to full &quot;health&quot; and it grows back. I would think that any exalt is pretty damn immune to any normal wear and tear, such as eating coarse food or developing arthritis for instance.<br /> <br /> I mean, if the exalts body can regrow damage to internal organs or entire chunks of meat being cut from them during the course of a battle, its entirely plausible they can just regrow teeth as well. I would think it more than a little strange if that was not the case.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T07:48:19-07:00","id":1068008,"title":"","content":"No. Teeth are the notable exception. Orchicalcum dentures were a common wonder in the First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T08:09:00-07:00","id":1068011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1067994#post1067994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there has to be <i>some</i> differences between how dragonblooded reproduction works and how it works in real like because IRL finite eggs are a thing, so the only way to avoid them going through the menopause at what is for them a really young age is either to say that they get infinitely renewing eggs or drastically reduce the frequency of periods, which would mean the window for conception would be so difficult to hit randomly that they'd probably have to go into heat or something, which is just opening an entirely <i>new</i> can of worms.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWomen <i>do</i> have a finite number of eggs, but the loss of fertility isn't because they run out, it's because after a certain period of time the unused ones wither.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe number of eggs a woman's ovaries contain is about a million, while only 500 actually get deposited in the uterus, and the rest go to waste. If we assumed that their oocytes were hardy enough to last indefinitely, a woman would have enough to ovulate for more than eighty thousand years.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T08:21:23-07:00","id":1068015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations?p=1068007#post1068007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if the exalts body can regrow damage to internal organs or entire chunks of meat being cut from them during the course of a battle, its entirely plausible they can just regrow teeth as well. I would think it more than a little strange if that was not the case.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, how much meat are you talking there? Barring additional magic, the Exalted don't regrow severed limbs.<br /> <br /> \u200bI wouldn't find it very off for lacerations to close up and teeth to remain gone, because organ tissues are made from cells that are capable of replication, as well as containing the means to form collagen that can patch over damage, while the enamel of teeth are chunks of mineral with no collagen. There's a reason why teeth are the only tissue in the human body that is never capable of healing; if you get a cut, your body is equipped to stitch that all back together eventually, but a cavity or crack in the enamel is irreversible, which is why we need dentists to put in artificial substances to patch them over.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, when it comes to the Exalted, I assume that when most of them lose teeth it's for good, because dentures are cool. I think they're just hardy enough to resist natural wear and tear and plaques have a hard time eating through them, but a hard blow or somebody yanking their teeth out as a form of torture means that they're going to need to get ivory from some suitably impressive local animal to construct a replacement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T11:40:57-07:00","id":1068060,"title":"","content":"Exalted are generally fairly hardy and resistant to disease, so I imagine it's fairly uncommon for an Exalt to get cavities or gingivitis provided they make even a token attempt at keeping their mouth clean. But getting your teeth knocked out in a fight is something else entirely and it just doesn't seem reasonable to me for an Exalt to regrow their teeth without some kind of magic to assist them. Even if such magic does exist, it's probably rare enough that most simply make do with a fake replacement tooth because, as Isator said, dentures are kind of cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T01:32:40-07:00","id":1068219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thousand_Comforts_Base</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1066765-dragon-blooded-families-lifespans-and-generations#post1066765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say 1 in 5 exalts, and ignore the other 4 because they're not relevant to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they are relevant to this. The offspring who don't exalt will grow up, marry, have children of their own, <i>grow old</i>, and fade away. Their children, and children's children, will too, and so on, until exaltation happens again sometime down the lineage.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo you have a stream of generations of mortal dynasts passing by, marking time, with the exalted branch occasionally stepping up onto the shore. Asking which generation you are, to the exalted, probably means more &quot;in which decade did you exalt?&quot;, and less, &quot;how many ancestors between you and our common ancestress?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bThough on the other hand there might be a mark of pride in noting <i>how few </i>mortal ancestors are in the lineage, it could be considered crass to mention it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 03-26-2017, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}